nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =-3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-2)\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (3)+(-2)\\cdot (2) \\\\  & =6 - 9 - 4 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546114 1080 "-12" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546114 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546114 1083 #uuid "857a1876-c6e3-5505-9faa-9ecd990ae58a" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546115 1080 "9" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546115 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546115 1083 #uuid "892a708e-7b21-5efd-a84f-5ffafb289617" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546116 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546119 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546116 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546116 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (x)+(-1)\\cdot (z)+(2)\\cdot (y),$ where $x=t + 3 s$, $y=s - t$, $z=- 3 s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546116 1072 #uuid "8e3a4bcf-977b-579b-8b15-e3ddf5401153" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546116 1074 "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-1)\\cdot (3)+(2)\\cdot (1)+(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3 + 2 + 3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546114 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546121 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546123 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546125 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1075 #edb/ref 17592186546130 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1077 "selection" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1078 #edb/ref 17592186546121 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546117 1079 #uuid "935c08d8-4b0b-5756-9deb-58e791d8fbfd" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546118 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546108 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546118 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546118 1071 "Let $f(x,y,z)=(-1)\\cdot (y)+(2)\\cdot (x)+(3)\\cdot (z),$ where $x=t - 3 s$, $y=- t - 2 s$, $z=- s + 2 t$. Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546118 1072 #uuid "a14e747f-884d-5e7d-bb04-a68302f8fbf5" 13194139535944 17592186045443 true] [17592186546118 1074 "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}